{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/923648-innocents-in-the-world-of-darkness","id":923648,"title":"innocents in the world of darkness","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-29T19:55:27-07:00","id":923648,"title":"innocents in the world of darkness","content":"i noticed there is no Sub-Forum for it, i was thinking about buying it. Can anyone give me some information on it and give me their opinion on if it's worth getting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-29T21:18:31-07:00","id":923693,"title":"","content":"WOD: Innocents is a blue book (general supplement rather than one for a specific supernatural game line) for Chronicles of Darkness 1e.<br /> <br /> I wasn't a huge fan of a lot of the mechanics (though if you're using 2e a good number of them don't matter anymore as it is), however the content is very strong. It is very specific though. If you want a book to help play children in the CofD in both theme and how to address using children is such a dark world, it's got a ton of good advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T09:06:04-07:00","id":923887,"title":"","content":"i haven't gotten any 2e books yet, i currently own Mage the awakening, Vampire the requiem, Werewolf the forsaken, Promethean the created, Hunter the vigil, as well as the Armory/Armory reloaded books and the original core book for the new World of darkness but it's all currently 1e.<br /> <br /> \u200binnocents seems like it could provide a good challenge which is exactly what i am looking for at the moment, dying is okay and sometimes even welcome as long as the adventure was fun. Do children have their own character sheets or do we simply use the regular one for mortal adults?<br /> <br /> Our group might move onto 2e books eventually but we are already so familiar with the system we have already been playing and wouldn't know what to do with all our current 1e books. Still, things like Beast do look pretty tempting to try out.<br /> <br /> Anyway, does anyone else have any more insight on innocents whether it be opinions or just basic information in general. The more details the better, anything anyone has to say would be much appreciated. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:32:08-07:00","id":923938,"title":"","content":"Innocents does indeed have its own character sheets, though you can still use the standard versions as long as you remember that things like attributes and skills are scaled down a bit for child characters compared to the assumed default of playing adults or teens.<br /> <br /> As a fan of book series like Goosebumps and My Teacher is an Alien growing up, Innocents does a pretty good job of scratching that itch for the WoD, at least in my opinion. There's a decent collection of NPCs and plot hooks covering a number of scenarios (including examples of the various supernatural splats to introduce as either allies or antagonists) and essays from the writers that explore things like how kids react differently than adults to frightening or dangerous situations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:43:29-07:00","id":923954,"title":"","content":"That sounds fun, i am probably going to get it then. Could someone direct me to a link where i could look at or even print out character sheets for children?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T10:48:55-07:00","id":923957,"title":"","content":"I always suggest checking Mr. Gone's stuff. here: <a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/nwod.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/nwod.html</a>, part way down the page is a section for Innocents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-30T11:01:38-07:00","id":923966,"title":"","content":"Thank you, Mr. Gone is a true hero","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12063-seta143","name":"Seta143","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-01T14:06:05-07:00","id":924608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/923648-innocents-in-the-world-of-darkness?p=923693#post923693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">WOD: however the content is very strong. It is very specific though. If you want a book to help play children in the CofD in both theme and how to address using children is such a dark world, it's got a ton of good advice.</div> </div> </div> </div> I strongly agree with this and frequently use the Steven King's '<i>It</i>' style childhood preludes to my main Chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkennes